backups/

# Deploy logs are RETAINED ON DISK deliberately (scripts/deploy-prod.sh writes
# the full transcript there, never piped through `tail`) but are not versioned:
# they are an operational record of one host, not source. See runbook §2.
docs/deploy-logs/

# The FOUNDATION runner's per-session transcripts (scripts/foundation-loop.sh).
# Same reasoning as the deploy logs — an operational record of one host, not
# source. ⚠️ AND NOT VERSIONING THEM IS LOAD-BEARING, not tidiness: the runner
# writes this file as its FIRST act, so without this rule every loop session
# after the first opens on a dirty tree — and MASTER.md STEP 0.2 tells that
# session to reconcile the tree "before anything else". The loop would spend
# each run triaging its own exhaust. `logs/.gitkeep` keeps the directory.
docs/foundation/logs/*.log

.design-preview-phase-6.html

