# Never a secret in a compose override. The QA stack already reads
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the shell (docker-compose.qa.yml); there is no reason
# for a key to be written to a file in the repo at all.
docker-compose.*key*.yml

# FOUNDATION session scratch, written to the repo root as `.<item>-<purpose>`
# (.b6-mutate.py, .b7s2-wait.py, .a1-probe.py …).
#
# This dirt is EXPLAINED by contract, not accidental: MASTER.md's CLOSE-OUT makes
# every session list its scratch by absolute path before its marker, under
# "SCRATCH — I cannot reap; this is for a supervised session", and a supervised
# session reaps it at pickup. It is declared when it is created and removed by a
# person who read the declaration.
#
# The loop's startup guard refuses to launch on a non-empty `git status
# --porcelain`, and it exists to catch dirt NOBODY declared — a half-applied edit
# that compiles, a stray file from a session that died. Leaving declared scratch
# visible does not make that guard stricter, it makes it noisier: the one signal
# it has gets buried under files the programme deliberately left behind. Ignoring
# them sharpens the signal rather than weakening it — whatever the guard reports
# after this is, by construction, something nobody explained.
.b[0-9]*-*
.t[0-9]*-*
.a[0-9]*-*
# ⚠️ `.f<N>-*` for the FIDELITY arc (F1…F5), added when F2 needed a probe and
# found no declared pattern for its own item prefix. The dash is load-bearing —
# `.f2probe.ts` does NOT match, and an undeclared file at the repo root is what
# once left the loop unable to relight ("REFUSING TO START — the working tree is
# dirty") over scratch it was not permitted to reap.
.f[0-9]*-*

# ⚠️ AND THE CLASS, NOT THE NEXT PREFIX — 2026-08-28, after the THIRD blocked
# relight in one day. `.f[0-9]*-*` encodes an assumption that worktrees are named
# after F-items. The ruling arc broke it (`.r1-fence`, `.r23-fix`) and so did a
# plain noun (`.judge`, no digit, no dash). Each time the loop's launch guard —
# which counts UNTRACKED files — refused to start over scratch it cannot reap.
#
# ⚠️ THE OBVIOUS FIX IS THE DANGEROUS ONE. A blanket `.*/` would ignore
# `.github/`, `.claude/` and `.agents/`, which are TRACKED. Already-tracked files
# would survive, but every NEW workflow or agent file would land ignored and
# silently never be committed. So the pattern is broad AND the three tracked
# directories are re-included immediately below, where the next reader meets them
# in the same breath as the rule that would have eaten them.
#
# ⚠️ IGNORED IS NOT ACCOUNTED-FOR. This pattern stops a worktree BLOCKING a
# relight; it also hides it from `git status`, which is how `.f5i2-queue` sat
# attached to a merged branch unnoticed. `bash scripts/list-worktrees.sh` is the
# other half — it lists every worktree WITH its merge state, so "invisible to
# status" never again means "gone".
.[a-z][a-z0-9]*-*/
.[a-z][a-z0-9]*/
!.github/
!.claude/
!.agents/

# ⚠️ THE LOOP HALT SWITCH IS LOCAL, NEVER TRACKED. A committed STOP halts the
# FOUNDATION loop in every clone and on every future checkout — and it arrives
# through `git add -A` in a session that had it sitting untracked, which is
# exactly how it reached `main` in c86f0a9e on 2026-08-14.
docs/foundation/STOP

# python bytecode from ad-hoc imports of scripts/lib/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
